      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Anesthesia Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"An anesthesia consent form is the patient's signed agreement to a specific anesthetic plan, such as general anesthesia or monitored anesthesia care. It names who will give the anesthetic and records that the risks and alternatives were explained. ANZCA expects it to carry a signature of its own, apart from the consent for the operation.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the anesthetic plans and the pre-op questions first, starting from the wording your hospital already uses. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> builds the form from that wording, along with the check-in screen and a list of every signed copy.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long is an anesthesia consent form good for?\", \"a\": \"Your facility's policy sets the limit, and the form should record the date and the case it covers. In hospitals, CMS requires a pre-anesthesia evaluation within 48 hours before surgery. Signing the consent at that visit keeps the two dates close, and a case that moves gets both again. Emergent can build the form to store each signed consent with its date in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I turn a paper anesthesia consent form template into an online form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Paste the template's wording, or the text of an anesthesia consent form PDF, into Emergent and it builds the form, with a risk section for each plan and a signature step. Keep the layout your providers already know. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/consent'>consent form</a> works the same way for other agreements.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a patient sign the anesthesia consent form?\", \"a\": \"Before any sedative premedication. Consent needs capacity, and medicine that alters mental status can take it away. ANZCA warns against asking a patient to sign after sedative premedication has been given. Schedule the anesthesia signature at the pre-op visit, never in the procedure room.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes an anesthesia consent form valid?\", \"a\": \"Capacity, disclosure, and voluntariness, and the form can show each one. A risk section written for the chosen plan covers disclosure, a signature taken before any sedative protects capacity, and a line saying the patient may decline speaks to voluntariness. ANZCA adds that a signature without the conversation is not consent.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who signs an anesthesia consent form as the provider?\", \"a\": \"The anesthesia provider, not the surgeon. AANA lists obtaining informed consent for anesthesia among a CRNA's duties before a procedure. When an anesthesiologist supervises, your group's policy says which of the two signs as the provider.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one anesthesia consent form also cover the operation?\", \"a\": \"It can share a page, but anesthesia still needs a signature of its own. ANZCA accepts a single form when anesthesia has a separate signature or acknowledgment. Hospital Conditions of Participation also require a properly executed consent in the chart before surgery, except in emergencies. A surgery consent form covers the operation itself.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does an anesthesia consent form record express or implied consent?\", \"a\": \"Express consent. Consent can be given in words or in writing, or implied by actions, and a signed anesthesia consent form puts it in writing. The patient signs after hearing the risks and the other options, which makes it informed consent too.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an anesthesia consent form ask pre-anesthesia questions?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add a fasting time and a question about family history of problems with anesthesia. Malignant hyperthermia, for example, is an inherited disorder triggered by volatile anesthetic gases and succinylcholine. Ask Emergent for a rule that flags an answer like that for the anesthesiologist before the day of the case.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ac8a0256cea93e7ab27259d",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Client Onboarding Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a client onboarding questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"A client onboarding questionnaire is the set of questions a business sends a new client before work begins. It gathers the company background, goals, key contacts, and anything the team needs access to. The best ones ask only what the team needs to begin.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a client onboarding questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Write down what the work cannot start without, then describe those questions and the follow-up you want to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the questionnaire, the reminders, and the table where each client's answers live. To change a question later, ask for it in plain words.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a client onboarding questionnaire include?\", \"a\": \"Start with who the main contact is and who approves work. Then ask what a good result looks like in 90 days and which accounts you will need access to. It also pays to ask what went wrong with the last provider. A bookkeeping firm adds questions on how the books are kept today.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free client onboarding questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Form builders and agency software companies publish free versions you can copy. Treat any client onboarding questionnaire template as a first draft. Cut each question nobody will act on in the first two weeks, then add the account access your service needs.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a client onboarding questionnaire example look like?\", \"a\": \"A good one fits on a few phone screens. A managed IT provider's version asks how many staff and devices the client has and who holds admin rights. It ends with the last outage that cost the client a full workday. A marketing agency would swap those for brand voice and ad account access.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I use a client onboarding questionnaire template?\", \"a\": \"Treat it as a list of questions to choose from, not as the finished form. Paste the ones you keep into a prompt and mark which are required, and Emergent builds an online form that saves each answer against the client. That beats emailing a client onboarding questionnaire PDF, which comes back as an attachment someone has to retype.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you send a new client questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Send it as soon as the contract is signed, while the client is keen to get going. Ask for it back a few days before the kickoff call. Answers in hand before the meeting let you spend the call on decisions instead of collecting facts. Built on Emergent, the questionnaire can email a reminder two days before the call to any client whose answers are still missing.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a client onboarding form different from a questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Mostly in depth. A client onboarding form often stops at contact and billing details, while a questionnaire covers goals, audience, and the history of the account. Many teams send both as one link. When a firm screens a prospect before taking them on, it calls that first step an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/intake'>intake form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a photography client questionnaire ask?\", \"a\": \"A photography client questionnaire should ask what the photos are for and where they will run, since a website banner and a square post crop differently. Then ask for locations, who will be in frame and any must-have shots. Weddings get their own wedding photography questionnaire.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes in a social media marketing client questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the brand voice, the target audience, the competitor accounts the client watches, and posts that worked before. Request access through each platform's business settings and never ask for a password. Agencies that also build sites follow up with a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/website-design-questionnaire'>website design questionnaire</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ace21b724c16292a769cba0",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Consent Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is the consent form?\", \"a\": \"A consent form is the document a person reads and signs before agreeing to a medical procedure or a research study. It explains what will happen and what could go wrong, and it says they may refuse. The signature records the decision and when it was made.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make my own consent form?\", \"a\": \"Start with the facts the signer needs, purpose and risks first, plus how to withdraw. Paste that text into Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> and describe who signs. It builds an online consent form that collects initials and a signature, then emails each signer a PDF copy.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an example of a consent form?\", \"a\": \"A dental extraction consent is a familiar consent form example: it names the tooth, lists risks such as dry socket and ends with a signature. Hospitals use a surgery consent form in the same way. In research, participants sign an informed consent form before they enroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a signed consent form?\", \"a\": \"A signed consent form is the completed copy: the text a person read, with a signature and a date at the bottom. It is what a clinic or study pulls out when someone later asks who agreed to what. Emergent keeps each one in a database you own, where staff can look it up by name or date.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the two forms of consent?\", \"a\": \"Express and implied. Express consent is stated outright, out loud or on paper, as when a patient signs before an extraction. Implied consent is read from behavior: a patient who rolls up a sleeve when the nurse lifts the flu shot. Any form of consent that may need proving later belongs in writing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an informed consent form?\", \"a\": \"An informed consent form records that a person understood the choice before signing, with the risks and the other options explained above the signature line. A simpler consent, such as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/photo-release'>photo release form</a>, may record only a yes. The person also gets time to ask questions before deciding.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an IRB consent form need to include?\", \"a\": \"An IRB consent form needs every element the federal Common Rule requires, in text the board approved before the first participant signs. Store the approval date with each version, and let participants sign only the current one. Studies with minors add a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/parent-consent'>parent consent form</a> and the child's assent. A study that enrolls thousands hits no response cap on Emergent.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an online consent form be signed electronically?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Federal research rules allow a consent form to be signed in an electronic format. In practice that is a finger on a phone screen or a mouse on a laptop. A digital consent form should save the time of each signature along with the signer's name. Outside research, confirm the rules for your field and state before relying on it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an ethical consent form?\", \"a\": \"An ethical consent form makes saying no as simple as saying yes. It explains the study or procedure in plain words and asks without pressure. It also states that refusing costs the person nothing. In a consent form app, the decline button sits beside the accept button, and a withdrawal is one tap away.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you make a consent form in Spanish?\", \"a\": \"Whenever a US study enrolls people who read Spanish better than English: consent information has to be in language the participant understands. Have the IRB approve the Spanish text, then build both versions into one form. Each signer picks a language, and the record notes which one they signed.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf53eaabe6b6cf736ce45b",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Driver Application Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a driver application form?\", \"a\": \"It is the application a carrier collects before someone drives for it. For drivers of commercial motor vehicles, 49 CFR 391.21 sets the minimum contents, from license details to a signed statement that the answers are true.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build a driver application form template?\", \"a\": \"Describe your fleet and the licenses you hire for to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds a driver application form template with screening rules and an applicant database, and you change any question by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does the federal government publish a driver application form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as a sample. FMCSA posts a free driver employment application that follows the federal list in 49 CFR 391.21. Carriers may use any layout instead. Whatever template you pick, confirm it asks for employers from the past 3 years plus every commercial driving job in the 7 years before them.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a paper driver application form enough?\", \"a\": \"For the rule itself, yes. A paper or PDF driver application form satisfies 49 CFR 391.21 once it is complete and signed. The trouble comes later: nobody hears that an applicant lacks an endorsement, and MVR orders end up in a separate spreadsheet. An app Emergent builds can alert the recruiter when an application arrives without the endorsement the job needs.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a driver application form used for non-CDL drivers too?\", \"a\": \"Often, yes. FMCSA's driver rules begin at 10,001 pounds for vehicles in interstate commerce, while a CDL begins at 26,001 pounds. Someone driving a 16,000-pound straight truck between states needs the full application and no CDL.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which license fields does a commercial driver application form include?\", \"a\": \"Each license held, with its number and the state that issued it, plus the expiration date. Most carriers also ask for the class and endorsements, because the freight decides whether a driver needs H for hazmat or N for tankers.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions go on a blank driver application form?\", \"a\": \"The federal list sets the sections. Identity details and 3 years of addresses come first. Work history and the crash and ticket record for the last 3 years take the most room. One box asks whether any license was ever denied, suspended, or revoked.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a driver application form include that a job application does not?\", \"a\": \"The driving record. A driver application form adds each license and its expiration date, the accidents and violations of the past 3 years, and commercial driving jobs going back 10 years. Office and warehouse roles use a standard <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/job-application'>job application form</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can applicants fill out a driver application form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Under 49 CFR 390.32, records a carrier must keep may be electronic, and an applicant may sign electronically. Emergent can build the form with e-signature capture and save each signed copy to a database you own. Within 30 days the carrier still needs driving records and previous-employer answers, often requested with a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/background-check'>background check form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a driver application form include drug and alcohol history?\", \"a\": \"Indirectly. Previous-employer inquiries cover DOT drug and alcohol violations, and FMCSA-regulated carriers run that check through the Drug and Alcohol Clearinghouse. The driver approves the query inside the Clearinghouse, apart from any drug test consent form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
